    "result_text": "Patron shares are in, and all 4 acceptance tests pass with `bin/e2e`.\n\nThe only file I changed is `src/main/frontend/src/app/features/people/people.ts`. I didn't change the database or the server. A person's shares depend only on how many patrons they have and the order they were named, and the server already sends the patrons in that order. So the screen works out the shares itself, the same way it already worked out backing.\n\n- **Shares:** each patron gets 100.00 divided by the number of patrons, rounded half to even. Whatever is left over from 100.00 goes to the first-named patron. With three patrons that gives 33.34, 33.33 and 33.33.\n- **Patrons cell:** shows `<name> <share>`, sorted by name and separated by commas, e.g. `Ben 33.34, Cam 33.33, Dot 33.33`.\n- **Backing:** each patron's settled figure from the last 90 days times their share divided by 100, added up and then rounded half to even once at the end. It uses whole-number arithmetic throughout so no rounding errors creep in.\n\nAdding a patron changes every share that person already has. Because shares are never stored, nothing has to be recalculated or rewritten in the database when that happens, including when two people are merged.\n\nThe original database migration (`V22__person_patron.sql`) still has a comment saying backing is the patrons' due-totals added up. I left it alone because changing a migration that has already run would make Flyway reject it at startup.",
